    "id": "coax_segment",
    "name": "Cryogenic coaxial segment",
    "category": "wiring",
    "parent": "wiring",
    "function": "One stage-to-stage run of semi-rigid coax. Material is the design choice: stainless steel (0.86 mm) between 300 K and 4 K because its low thermal conductivity limits the conducted load; cupronickel below 4 K; and superconducting NbTi on the output line between the mixing chamber and the HEMT, where the signal is a few photons and any resistive loss costs readout fidelity. Its attenuation is lumped at the cold end for the noise budget.",
